      "raw": "<p>Hello, the following situation happened:</p><p>Benchmark has 2 software cards in play and 1 hardware card:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/QjA9sXv\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/QjA9sXv</a></p><p>Each software card says: &bdquo;At the start of your turn, if you have more software than hardware in play, draw a card and destroy 2 software card.&ldquo; Therefore a card was drawn:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/d3YLE06\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/d3YLE06</a></p><p>Now both software cards have to be destroyed:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/pGZzOKc\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/pGZzOKc</a></p><p>Ally Matrix was chosen:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/mJFf5I5\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/mJFf5I5</a></p><p>Now the bug occured, a least I think it is a bug. Instead of destroying the other software card (Load On Initialization), its start of turn effect resolves:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/Fhcl6dR\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/Fhcl6dR</a></p><p>I drew a card:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/OVPJZUm\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/OVPJZUm</a></p><p>No second software card was destroyed and it&lsquo;s my play phase:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/6P6BwPB\" style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://imgur.com/a/6P6BwPB</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think both software cards should&lsquo;ve been destroyed without Load On Initialization interrupting. After the effect of Load On Interruption the card checks again if the criteria software cards &lt;= hardware cards is fulfilled which applied and no second software card (the card itself) was destroyed.&nbsp;</p><p>Am I wrong?</p>",
