    {
      "id": 220330,
      "name": "Dr. Kaylo Epsilon",
      "username": "Dr_Kaylo_Epsilon",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dr_kaylo_epsilon/{size}/2024_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-26T03:36:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For what it’s worth, I’m not a playtester and my reactions when I stumbled upon this during play were:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Oh, right. I only lost one software because I destroyed the source of the destruction effect before it could knock out more software. Of course.</li>\n<li>Hmm, and that works thematically, too. If you shut down processes overloading your system ASAP, you can keep the system running near peak capacity. If you defer maintenance, thing always blow up worse.</li>\n<li>Now, what order should I redeploy software in to maximize the benefit I get from carefully ordered shutdown of processes.</li>\n<li>Muahahaha Benchmark draws so many cards under a Fixed Point!!!</li>\n</ol>\n<p>So, not a playtester, but also not fazed by the behavior.<br>\n(Though I can totally see it puzzling a new player; I’m not denying that point.)</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:52:48.602Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
